From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000105 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 12:01:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: enable legacy Gemini DA9214 after
 handoff

Candidate AR proved the DVFSP/I2C6 ownership boundary with a childless
controller: I2C_APPM is gated and the shared AP_DMA gate remains unchanged in
all 32 samples. Restore only the documented I2C6 electrical properties and
the exact two-output legacy DA9214 description so the fail-closed regulator
probe can exercise one read-only identification path.

The access-controller dependency remains mandatory. No A72 power consumer,
regulator supply, boot-on/always-on policy, voltage request, or enable GPIO is
added.

---
 .../boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
@@ -224,4 +224,23 @@
 &i2c6 {
 	access-controllers = <&dvfsp_handoff>;
 	status = "okay";
+	clock-frequency = <3400000>;
+	mediatek,use-push-pull;
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&i2c6_pins_a>;
+
+	da9214: regulator@68 {
+		compatible = "dlg,da9214";
+		reg = <0x68>;
+
+		regulators {
+			da9214_bucka: BUCKA {
+				regulator-name = "da9214-bucka";
+			};
+
+			da9214_buckb: BUCKB {
+				regulator-name = "vproc-big";
+			};
+		};
+	};
 };
-- 
